## Interface: 16001, 120105
## Title: |cffC9A24ATwich|rUI Layout Setup
## Notes: The setup wizard for TwichUI's interface layouts. Loaded only when you open it (/tui layout); keep it turned on alongside TwichUI.
## Author: twichie
## Version: 1.0.0
## RequiredDeps: !!!TwichUI, TwichUI_Layouts
## LoadOnDemand: 1
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\!!!TwichUI\media\icon
## X-License: MIT (code); see !!!TwichUI\LICENSE
## Category: Interface Enhancements

# docs/layouts/wizard.md has what it does. It keeps no saved variables of its own: the choices it remembers are TwichUIDB.layouts.wizard
# (the core's), and the install record is TwichUIDB.layouts.install, written by TwichUI_Layouts. Nothing here runs until the window is asked for.
# Artwork (media/*.tga) is made by tools/make_layout_wizard_art.py from the sources in assets/; a missing file never stops the wizard.
Art.lua

# Remembered choices, then the model (no frames: what each step shows and what its buttons do), then the drawing
State.lua
Scene.lua
Model.lua
Preview.lua
Pages.lua
Overlay.lua

# The authoring workspace (for the person who makes a layout; /tui layout author): its model, then its window. Nothing is built
# until it is opened.
Author.lua
AuthorPresets.lua
AuthorWindow.lua

# The window (last: it tells TwichUI the wizard is ready)
Window.lua
